From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:36:37 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Video layer: frames turned ahead of the display's turn in
 landscape

The display took the video panel as a hardware overlay in portrait and
composed it on the GPU in landscape, the panel arranged the same way: in
landscape the system turns the app's picture a quarter turn for the
natively portrait display. The shell now says how far the display turns
(gecko_w10m_video_layer_rotation), the layer turns each frame by that much
on the D3D11 video processor while copying it into a chain of the swapped
size, and passes the turn with the placement so the shell turns the panel
back; the system is left nothing to turn. A video processor that cannot
turn frames leaves them as they come, with a note saying why.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../GeckoW10mVideoLayer.cpp                   | 267 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 258 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

